## SQ-CBP-01 | chain: absent-mods lines print, loot tables of absent mods parse
@group B (chain)
@commands `port_chain.sh server OUT cbp01 A chain`; boot; `grep -h "absent mods" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/latest.log`; `grep -cE "Couldn't parse loot table\|Can't find block" logs/latest.log`
@pass one `[absent mods] loot tables: ...` line (counts per mod: fruitsdelight, moredelight, supplementaries, upgrade_aquatic, endersdelight among them); recipe and tag `[absent mods]` lines or `none skipped` printed after the recipe event (no longer missing); loot parse errors 0
@fails `LootTablesOptionalModsMixin` not applied (mixin log) or the print still in `afterRecipes`
@from batches/r1106cbp/p1_chain.qb
shell grep -h "absent mods" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/latest.log | sed -E 's/^\[[^]]*\] \[[^]]*\]: //'
bootexpect \[absent mods\] loot tables: .* left out by forge:conditions
kjsexpect \[absent mods\] (skipped [0-9]+ .* rows for absent|none skipped)
shell n=$(grep -cE "Couldn't parse loot table|Can't find block" logs/latest.log); echo "loot errors=$n"; test "$n" = 0
shell grep -E "Couldn't parse loot table" logs/latest.log | grep -oE "loot table [a-z_:/.0-9]+" | sort | uniq | head -40
look the loot-table line names fruitsdelight, moredelight, supplementaries, upgrade_aquatic, endersdelight among others

## SQ-CBP-02 | cooking: no Empty array?, IE empty-output prune line, failures under 40
@group B (cooking set)
@commands `port_chain.sh server OUT cbp02 A cooking`; boot; `grep -h "Empty array" logs/kubejs/*.log logs/latest.log \| wc -l`; `grep -h "\[NCH\] removed" logs/kubejs/*.log`; failures total as in SQ-CBC-02
